            "Everything is structured data",
            "Everything is big data regardless of form",
            "Classification does not matter"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "why": "Structured data fits relational tables; semi-structured (JSON logs) has tags but no fixed schema; unstructured (images, video) has no predefined model. The classification drives storage, tooling, and analysis choices.",
          "hint": "Which dataset fits neatly in rows and columns?",
          "objectives": [
            "Data types",
            "Structured vs unstructured"
